{
  "_note": "Ours, not a ComfyUI export and not a template: no shipped template outpaints with Flux 2 (the only outpaint examples on this box are flux_fill_outpaint_example and Wan VACE, both for other models). It is image_flux2_klein_edit-api.json - same loaders, same 4 steps, same euler, same CFG 1 - with the sampling latent swapped: ImagePadForOutpaint grows the canvas and hands its own mask to VAEEncodeForInpaint, so only the new border is denoised and the original is carried through untouched, while the ReferenceLatent pair still sees the *clean* unpadded picture so the model knows what it is continuing. Every input name and default checked against GET /object_info. **feathering is 0 on purpose**: the node's default 40 feathers the mask, VAEEncodeForInpaint then blends grey into those half-masked pixels, and the first render came back with a bright grey band across the sky where the old top edge was. At 0, grow_mask_by 6 does the softening in the latent instead and the band is gone - both renders are in CLAUDE.md. Verified on 2026-09-15: 1280x704 padded 25% all round came back 1600x880 with the field and sky continued convincingly in 6s at a 15837 MiB peak. The node map is in CLAUDE.md.",
